---
/**
 * Privacy Policy — standalone legal page.
 *
 * Serves two purposes:
 *   1. The "Privacy Policy URL" required by App Store Connect for the iOS and
 *      macOS apps (https://pippinplayer.com/privacy).
 *   2. The canonical source of the copy that is pasted into App Store Connect's
 *      tvOS privacy-policy TEXT field (Apple TV has no browser, so the text is
 *      entered directly there — keep the two in sync from this file).
 *
 * Content reflects the app's actual data flows (see the app's
 * PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy manifests): the app collects no data and does no
 * tracking; it talks to the user's own servers and, for metadata/subtitles,
 * to a few providers via the Pippin Cloudflare Worker (key injection only).
 * Casting invokes the Google Cast SDK, which collects its own diagnostics.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '29 July 2026';
const contactEmail = 'mail@pippinplayer.com';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Pippin"
  description="Pippin's privacy policy. Pippin collects no personal data and does not track you — it connects directly to the media servers you configure."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal" id="top">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <header class="legal__header reveal">
        <p class="legal__eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal__body reveal">
        <p class="legal__lede">
          Pippin is designed to keep your data yours. The app collects no
          personal information, contains no analytics or advertising, and does
          not track you across apps or websites. It connects directly to the
          media servers and services you choose to configure. This policy
          explains what that means in practice.
        </p>

        <h2>Who this applies to</h2>
        <p>
          This policy covers the Pippin apps for iPhone, iPad, Mac and Apple TV
          (&ldquo;Pippin&rdquo;, &ldquo;the app&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;) and
          this website. Pippin is a client for media servers such as
          <a href="https://www.plex.tv/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plex</a>
          and
          <a href="https://jellyfin.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jellyfin</a>.
          It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by Plex, Jellyfin,
          or any other third-party service.
        </p>

        <h2>Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>None.</strong> Pippin does not collect, transmit to us, or
          store on our servers any personal data. We do not operate accounts,
          we do not run analytics, and we have no advertising or tracking SDKs.
          We never receive your media library, viewing history, or server
          credentials.
        </p>

        <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Everything Pippin needs to work is kept locally on your device (and,
          where you enable it, in Apple&rsquo;s iCloud/keychain sync under your
          own Apple Account). This includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The servers and services you add, and their connection details.</li>
          <li>
            Sign-in credentials and access tokens, stored in the device
            keychain.
          </li>
          <li>
            Your app settings, layout customisations, and downloaded media for
            offline playback.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This data stays on your device. Deleting the app removes it. Your
          server credentials are sent only to the servers you configure, never
          to us.
        </p>

        <h2>Connections the app makes</h2>
        <p><strong>Your media servers.</strong> Pippin connects directly to the
          Plex, Jellyfin, and companion services (such as Overseerr/Jellyseerr,
          Radarr, and Sonarr) that you set up. Your credentials and requests go
          straight to those servers over your own network or the addresses you
          provide. We are not in the middle of these connections.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Sign-in.</strong> If you sign in with Plex, authentication is
          handled directly with Plex&rsquo;s own sign-in service under
          <a href="https://www.plex.tv/about/privacy-legal/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plex&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Artwork &amp; subtitles.</strong> To enrich metadata and find
          subtitles, Pippin may contact providers including
          <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TMDB</a>,
          fanart.tv, and subtitle services (Subdl / OpenSubtitles). To keep API
          keys out of the app, these requests are relayed through Pippin&rsquo;s
          Cloudflare Worker, which injects the relevant key and forwards the
          request. The Worker does not require or store any personal
          information about you; it passes along only the metadata query needed
          to fulfil the request (for example, a title or content identifier).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Casting.</strong> If you cast to a Chromecast or Google TV
          device, Pippin uses Google&rsquo;s Cast SDK to discover and control
          that device. The Cast SDK collects device identifiers, product
          interaction, and diagnostic data for its own operation, governed by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>.
          This happens only when you use casting. Pippin does not use this data
          and does not use it to track you.
        </p>

        <h2>Face ID / Touch ID</h2>
        <p>
          If you enable Pippin&rsquo;s profile lock, Face ID or Touch ID may be
          used to unlock a protected profile. This authentication is performed
          entirely by Apple on your device. Pippin never receives or stores your
          biometric data.
        </p>

        <h2>Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Pippin does not track you. We do not collect data to link your
          activity to you across other companies&rsquo; apps or websites, and we
          show no advertising. Pippin&rsquo;s App Tracking Transparency status is
          &ldquo;not used for tracking.&rdquo;
        </p>

        <h2>Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Pippin is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any
          information from anyone, including children under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Because we do not collect or hold any personal data about you, there
          is nothing for us to access, correct, or delete on our side. You
          remain in full control of the data stored on your device and on the
          servers you connect to. Questions about the data held by a connected
          service (Plex, Jellyfin, TMDB, Google, etc.) should be directed to
          that service under its own privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we will update the date at the top of this
          page. Material changes will be reflected here before they take effect.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-8)) var(--space-9);
  }
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .legal__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--label);
  }
  .legal__updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--label-tertiary);
  }

  .legal__body {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
  .legal__lede {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--label);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background-color: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }
  .legal__body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--label);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal__body p {
    color: var(--label-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .legal__body ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal__body li {
    color: var(--label-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .legal__body strong {
    color: var(--label);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal__body a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: opacity var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .legal__body a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
